within Pharmacolibrary.Drugs.R_RespiratorySystem.R03A_AdrenergicsInhalants.R03AC02_Salbutamol;
model Salbutamol "Salbutamol — default model: Salbutamol_Walsh2023_reference"
  extends Salbutamol_Walsh2023_reference;
  annotation (Documentation(info = "<html><body><p>The default model of salbutamol: <a href=\"modelica://Pharmacolibrary.Drugs.R_RespiratorySystem.R03A_AdrenergicsInhalants.R03AC02_Salbutamol.Salbutamol_Walsh2023_reference\">Salbutamol_Walsh2023_reference</a>, chosen among the models extracted from papers (reviewer verdict, ground-truth agreement, completeness). All models of salbutamol in this package:</p><ul><li><code>Salbutamol_Marques2024v2_reference</code></li><li><code>Salbutamol_Walsh2023_reference</code></li><li><code>Salbutamol_Walsh2023_PD_hr_z_score</code></li><li><code>Salbutamol_Walsh2023_PD_glucose</code></li></ul><h4>About salbutamol</h4><p>Salbutamol is a bronchodilator used to treat asthma, bronchospasm and other obstructive lung diseases. It is widely used worldwide, appears on the WHO list of essential medicines, and is available on prescription.</p><p><small>Summary written by glm-5.3-flash from <a href=\"https://www.wikidata.org/wiki/Q410358\">Wikidata Q410358</a> and the WHO ATC classification; not checked by a person.</small></p><p>Identity, molar mass and metabolites: <a href=\"modelica://Pharmacolibrary.Drugs.Substances.Salbutamol\">Salbutamol</a>.</p></body></html>", revisions = "<html><body><ul><li>10/2026 generated by pharmacolibrary-dev export.pharmacolibrary_models from default: parameters extracted from the paper by the pharmacolibrary-dev pipeline, model built by its engineer, reviewed: default</li></ul></body></html>"), experiment(StartTime = 0, StopTime = 86400, Tolerance = 1e-9, Interval = 1));
end Salbutamol;
